=== check
status: 1
--- stderr
error[E0601]: missing return: `sign` can reach its end without returning a string
  --> statements.dat:10:1
10 | }
   | ^ `sign` returns string
fix (review): return a value at the end of `sign`
10 |   return _;

error[E0652]: `report` returns void, so `return` can't have a value
  --> statements.dat:13:10
13 |   return n;
   |          ^
fix (review): return without a value
13 |   return;

error[E0201]: `limit` is const and can't be reassigned
  --> statements.dat:18:3
18 |   limit = 20;
   |   ^^^^^ declared with `const`
fix (review): declare it with `let`
17 |   let limit = 10;

error[E1402]: limit is already declared
  --> statements.dat:19:9
19 |   const limit = 30;
   |         ^^^^^ declared earlier in this scope

error[E0303]: ++ is a statement
  --> statements.dat:21:11
21 |   let j = i++;
   |           ^^^ `++` can't be used inside an expression
fix: move `i++` into its own statement
21 |   let j = i; i++;

error[E0304]: no prefix form: write `i++`
  --> statements.dat:22:3
22 |   ++i;
   |   ^^^ `++` goes after the variable
fix: use `i++`
22 |   i++;

error[E0750]: `continue` outside a loop
  --> statements.dat:23:3
23 |   continue;
   |   ^^^^^^^^^ there's no loop to leave here

error[E0204]: no type and no value
  --> statements.dat:24:3
24 |   let x;
   |   ^^^^^^ dat can't tell what type `x` has
fix (review): give it a value
24 |   let x = _;

error[E0205]: const must be initialized
  --> statements.dat:25:3
25 |   const y: int;
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
fix (review): give it a value
25 |   const y: int = _;

error[E0305]: `total == 5` has no effect
  --> statements.dat:31:3
31 |   total == 5;
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^ a statement must do something, such as assign, call or return
fix (review): assign with `=`
31 |   total = 5;

error[E0305]: `cap == 4` has no effect
  --> statements.dat:32:3
32 |   cap == 4;
   |   ^^^^^^^^ a statement must do something, such as assign, call or return
fix (review): remove the statement

error[E0305]: `total == total` has no effect
  --> statements.dat:33:3
33 |   total == total;
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a statement must do something, such as assign, call or return
fix (review): remove the statement

error[E0305]: `total` has no effect
  --> statements.dat:34:3
34 |   total;
   |   ^^^^^ a statement must do something, such as assign, call or return
fix (review): remove the statement

error[E0305]: `-total` has no effect
  --> statements.dat:35:3
35 |   -total;
   |   ^^^^^^ a statement must do something, such as assign, call or return
fix (review): remove the statement

error[E0305]: `total + 1 < 5` has no effect
  --> statements.dat:36:3
36 |   total + 1 < 5;
